 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«There is» and «to have»: 있어요 / 없어요",
     "texto": [
      "**있어요** means «there is» and also «I have». **없어요** is the opposite: «there isn't», «I don't have».",
      "What you have takes **이** (after a consonant) or **가** (after a vowel): 저는 동생**이** 있어요 (I have a younger brother). 저는 언니**가** 없어요 (I don't have an older sister).",
      "With a number: 오빠가 **한 명** 있어요 (I have an older brother)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Siblings",
     "texto": [
      "Korean does not just say «brother»: it depends on whether they are **older or younger** than you, and on whether **you** are a boy or a girl.",
      "A **boy** calls his older brother **형** and his older sister **누나**. A **girl** calls her older brother **오빠** and her older sister **언니**.",
      "Younger siblings are **동생**: 남동생 (younger brother) and 여동생 (younger sister)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Older siblings",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Older brother",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Older sister",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "if you are a boy",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "형",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "누나",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "if you are a girl",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "오빠",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "언니",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ]
     ],
     "nota": "",
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "우리 가족 and 제 가족",
     "texto": [
      "**우리** means «we» or «our», and it is used a lot to talk about your own family: **우리 가족**, **우리 어머니**. In that context it can be translated as «my family» or «my mother». It is not compulsory: **제 가족**, **제 어머니** are also correct; 제 is the polite form of «my». The choice depends on context and tone."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Answering a negative question",
     "texto": [
      "If someone asks you **동생은 없어요?** (don't you have any younger siblings?) and you don't have any, you can answer **네, 없어요**: «yes, that's right: I don't have». If you do have some, you answer **아니요, 있어요**: «no, it's not like that: I do have»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
